From: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 20:29:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] patch 1: DPP TLVF schema and BPL config plumbing

Add the yaml/config groundwork needed by later DPP patches:

- beerocks_message_action.yaml / beerocks_message_control.yaml: add
  cACTION_CONTROL_DPP_RADIO_INFO_NOTIFICATION, sent once per radio by
  DPP-onboarded agents (which skip WSC M1/M2 and therefore never send
  cACTION_CONTROL_SLAVE_JOINED_NOTIFICATION) so the controller can still
  populate interface name, bridge IPv4, and backhaul MAC for BML.
- son_wireless_utils.h: add eAdditionalAuth::DPP so per-VAP hostapd config
  can be scoped to BSSes actually configured for DPP onboarding.
- bpl_cfg.h / dm,linux,rdk,uci backends: add cfg_get_onboarding_type(),
  cfg_get_1905_security_enabled(); uci backend additionally persists the
  dpp/dpp_controller/dpp_configurator_connectivity UCI options and computes
  the DPP bootstrap public-key hash (cfg_get_dpp_bootstrap_pubkey_hash())
  used as hostapd's pkhash for dpp_controller.

Signed-off-by: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
